{"nodes": [{"id": "tz_overal_project_overview", "label": "UzCasting Project Overview (one page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "whole file", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single-page summary of what the product is, where the code lives, what is ready and what is blocking; explicitly not a greenfield project - the casting half already runs in production with a backend, site, Telegram bot and admin panel."}, {"id": "tz_overal_repository_structure", "label": "Repository Structure (mobile, backend, frontend, roadmap, tz, tools)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tz_overal_four_level_monetization", "label": "Four-Level Monetization (episode, premiere, Premium, Stars)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client's 13.08.2026 message overrides the spec's numbers: an episode is 3000 sum (not 5000), a whole premiere 15000, Premium runs 24000/49999/99000/159900 for 1/3/6/12 months, and Stars come in packages. Premium unlocks everything; per-episode and per-premiere purchases exist for people who will not subscribe. Premiere, Stars, rating and advertising appear nowhere in the spec - they all come from that message."}, {"id": "tz_overal_three_blockers", "label": "Three Blockers", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered by how badly each breaks the architecture or the economics: store billing, the unprotected API, and minors' personal data."}, {"id": "tz_overal_store_billing_risk", "label": "Store Billing Risk (15-30% commission)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Episodes, premieres, subscriptions and Stars are in-app digital content, so Google Play and the App Store require their own billing; using Click/Payme/Uzum for it breaks store rules and gets the app removed. The commission is taken before the 50/50 split, so on a 3000 sum episode the creator receives roughly 1050-1275 rather than 1500. Must be settled before the payment module is written."}, {"id": "tz_overal_minor_data_legal_risk", "label": "Minors' Personal Data Legal Risk", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The public endpoint returns phone, email, exact birth date and body measurements including profiles aged 17; the mobile app deliberately ignores those fields but the exposure is on the backend, making this a legal rather than technical problem."}, {"id": "tz_overal_client_questions", "label": "Twelve Questions to the Client", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Screens stay undesigned until these are answered: Stars pricing and whether Stars are creator income, whether a 15000 premiere covers future episodes, ad network, auto-renewal, 5000 vs 3000, Styling/Courses catalogs, 10 vs 4 categories actually present in the database, Latin vs Cyrillic, refund rules, DRM vs signed URLs, and verified badge criteria."}, {"id": "tz_overal_data_source_status", "label": "Data Source Status (real API vs placeholder)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "tz/overal.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Creators come from the real endpoint; 